cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DroneBioR: Reproducible Drone Biomass Workflows for Multispectral Imagery"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Hugo Machado"
    family-names: "Rodrigues"
    email: "rodrigues.machado.hugo@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "University of Florida, Range Cattle Research and Education Center (REC-Ona)"
abstract: >
  DroneBioR is an R package for reproducible drone biomass research with
  multispectral imagery from MicaSense cameras such as the RedEdge series.
  It wraps external photogrammetry engines (OpenDroneMap, WebODM,
  Pix4Dmapper, Agisoft Metashape) to obtain orthomosaics, DSM/DTM and
  dense point clouds, then provides the scientific layer in R: alpha and
  no-data masking, radiometric scaling to reflectance, nine vegetation
  indices, canopy height models, point-cloud ROI analysis, field sample
  extraction, baseline biomass models and a Shiny application for
  interactive exploration.
keywords:
  - drone
  - UAV
  - biomass
  - remote-sensing
  - multispectral
  - MicaSense
  - photogrammetry
  - vegetation-indices
  - R
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/HugoMachadoRodrigues/DroneBioR"
url: "https://github.com/HugoMachadoRodrigues/DroneBioR"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-05-11"
